# Never bake runtime data / models / caches into the trainer image.
# Compliance (env rules: no bundled dataset / no bundled model) + reproducibility.
# These are all generated or downloaded at RUNTIME (self-gen trajectories, the
# validator-provided task model, validator-whitelisted datasets, the leduc CFR
# solver cache) — never shipped in the image. They are gitignored too, but the
# Docker build context honors .dockerignore, so this is the belt-and-suspenders
# that guarantees a stray populated dir can't silently bake into a rebuild.
scripts/datasets/
scripts/models/

# Local-only measurement/verification tooling: NOT reachable from the tournament
# entrypoint (run_text_trainer.sh -> text_trainer.py). Verified by import-closure:
# 24 of 35 modules are reachable; everything under tools/ is not. These are run by
# hand on a dev box (eval_pvp_winrate, presubmit_check, combined_dryrun), so they
# must stay in the repo but must not be baked into the trainer image.
# NOTE: eval_pvp_winrate imports `from envs import ...`, so it only runs as
#   cd scripts && python -m tools.eval_pvp_winrate
# which is why tools/ stays inside scripts/ and is excluded here instead of moved.
scripts/tools/
scripts/envs/.expert_cache/
scripts/**/.expert_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.git/
.gitignore
*.log
